# PPT slide style (Title + Diagram only)

For session MDX slides intended for presenter mode:

1. Each slide must contain exactly:
   - one heading title (`## ...`), and
   - one visual/interactive component block (diagram/demo/simulator).
2. Do not add explanatory paragraph text under slide titles.
3. Do not place multiple diagram components under one title.
4. If two visuals are needed, split into two separate `##` headings (two slides).
5. Prefer concise, visual-first slide titles.

## Diagram clarity (must-follow)

Session diagrams and interactives should stay readable on video and in fullscreen presenter mode:

- **Fonts:** All interactives must follow `.cursor/rules/session-video-legibility.mdc` (body `text-lg md:text-xl`+, headings `text-xl md:text-2xl`+, no `text-xs` for teaching copy). SVG labels: 16px+ equivalent; prefer `ui-sans-serif` / system stacks; strong contrast on light and dark backgrounds.
- **Diagram:** Prefer generous padding inside the canvas, clear hierarchy (one main idea per slide), and labels that read without squinting.
- **Animation:** Motions should be easy to follow (predictable timing, not overcrowded); respect reduced motion where the component supports it.
- **Spacing:** Leave clear vertical space between the slide **`##` title** and the diagram — do not cram components directly under headings in MDX layouts; when building new components, assume titles need breathing room below.

Layout spacing for headings vs diagrams is enforced in `SessionSection` (presenter) and MDX `h2` styles (`app/sessions/[slug]/page.tsx`); new slide-style content must still avoid stacking extra elements between title and diagram.

When updating existing sessions, preserve this format for any newly added or edited slide content.
